{
  "_correction_2026_11_11": "POST-HOC FIELD CORRECTION, disclosed rather than silently re-run. The arms were measured with `true_patterns` = n_intents * n_patterns_per_intent (a product). That field was the WRONG REFERENCE FRAME: gt['pattern_id'] is a PER-INTENT label with exactly n_patterns_per_intent = 3 distinct values on all eight regimes (verified against data/bench_v1/*/gt.jsonl and reports/*/metrics.json -> clustering.n_true_patterns). The field has been renamed to n_true_patterns and set to 3 for all 16 arms (16 arms touched). NO MEASURED VALUE WAS CHANGED: ari_pattern_pool always compared against the correct per-intent labels, and no consumer reads this field -- capreport.py and asymreport.py both take n_true_patterns from reports/*/metrics.json. Re-running the 16 arms (1587 s) to regenerate a cosmetic field was judged not worth it; the correction is recorded here instead. The product is also not n_true_cells (R4: product 12, actual 11).",
  "_note": "cap from declaration (=5 on both shipped ontologies) vs cap 8 (what production gets if pattern_count is never wired). CLEAN regimes only; tierexp.py already covers the polluted case.",
